  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q12",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "$P(x)=2x^3-ax^2-bx-1$. The remainder is $-10$ when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x+1)$ and $-37$ when $P(x)$ is divided by $x+2$. Find $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3$, $b=-4$. Use $-a+b=-7$ and $-4a+2b=-20$.",
      "worked": "By the remainder theorem, $P(-1)=-10$ and $P(-2)=-37$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(-1)^3-a(-1)^2-b(-1)-1&=-10\\\\-a+b&=-7\\qquad(1)\\\\2(-2)^3-a(-2)^2-b(-2)-1&=-37\\\\-4a+2b&=-20\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nDouble (1):\n$$-2a+2b=-14\\qquad(3)$$\nSubtract (3) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}-2a&=-6\\\\a&=3\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}-3+b&=-7\\\\b&=-4\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
